@startuml history_flow
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam defaultFontName Microsoft YaHei,SimHei,sans-serif

title History Recording & Consumption Flow (intention #16)

actor "GameCore.play_round()" as GC
participant "Player\nhistory:\nlist[PlayerHistoryItem]" as Player
participant "CardResolver\n.get_consecutive_attack()" as Resolver
participant "GameCore\n.get_state()" as GS
participant "Converter\n.build_input_vector()" as Conv
participant "SessionStore\n_save/_load" as SS
participant "API / Frontend" as API

== Round Execution (Recording) ==

GC -> GC : 1. Validate cards
GC -> Resolver : 2. get_consecutive_attack(player.history)
Resolver -> Player : read .card from each item
Resolver --> GC : streak count
GC -> GC : 3. resolve(..., streak)
GC -> GC : 4-6. Apply damage, statuses, BUILD
GC -> Player : 7. history.append(\n  PlayerHistoryItem(card, build_target))
note right
  OLD: history.extend(cards)
       build_history.append(build_target)
  NEW: Single append with both fields
end note

== State Query (Consumption) ==

GC -> GS : get_state()
GS -> Player : Read history directly
note right
  OLD: zip(p.history, p.build_history)
       → construct PlayerHistoryItem
  NEW: p.history already list[PlayerHistoryItem]
end note
GS --> GC : state dict with history

GC -> Conv : build_input_vector(state)
Conv -> Conv : Read history[-1] → last action index
Conv --> GC : 15-d input vector

== Persistence ==

SS -> SS : _serialize_player(player)
note right
  OLD: {"history": ["attack", ...],
         "build_history": [null, ...]}
  NEW: {"history": [
         {"card": "attack",
          "build_target": null}, ...]}
  Removed: "build_history" key
end note

SS -> SS : _deserialize_player(data)
note right
  Deserialize history back to
  list[PlayerHistoryItem]
end note

== API Response ==

API -> API : Flask JSON encoding
note right
  PlayerHistoryItem → {"card": ..., "build_target": ...}
  Already handled by _custom_default encoder
end note

@enduml
